From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000012 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keystone P550 Integration <keystone-p550@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sm: restore Keystone PMP ownership after OpenSBI setup

OpenSBI 1.6 invokes the platform final-init hook before its final domain PMP
configuration.  The P550 hook initializes Keystone in final-init, so OpenSBI
subsequently overwrites the monitor's eight-entry PMP layout.  Expose an
idempotent per-hart restore operation for a post-OpenSBI hook.

Reserve the one remaining PMP entry for the complete EIC770X ACLINT window.
The resulting fixed layout consumes entries 0-4 and 7, leaving entries 5 and
6 for the enclave EPM and UTM.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [P550/OpenSBI integration]
---
 src/sm.c                     | 21 ++++++++++++---------
 src/sm.h                     |  1 +
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
diff --git a/src/sm.c b/src/sm.c
index 6a4ef73..ea773ae 100644
--- a/src/sm.c
+++ b/src/sm.c
@@ -160,21 +160,24 @@ void sm_init(bool cold_boot)
   }
 
   /* below are executed by all harts */
-  pmp_init();
-  pmp_set_keystone(sm_region_id, PMP_NO_PERM);
-  pmp_set_keystone(os_region_id, PMP_ALL_PERM);
-
-  /* Fire platform specific global init */
-  if (platform_init_global() != SBI_ERR_SM_ENCLAVE_SUCCESS) {
-    sbi_printf("[SM] platform global init fatal error");
-    sbi_hart_hang();
-  }
+  sm_restore_pmp();
 
   sbi_printf("[SM] Keystone security monitor has been initialized!\n");
 
   sm_print_hash();
 
   return;
   // for debug
   // sm_print_cert();
 }
+
+void sm_restore_pmp(void)
+{
+  pmp_init();
+  pmp_set_keystone(sm_region_id, PMP_NO_PERM);
+  pmp_set_keystone(os_region_id, PMP_ALL_PERM);
+  if (platform_init_global() != SBI_ERR_SM_ENCLAVE_SUCCESS) {
+    sbi_printf("[SM] platform global init fatal error");
+    sbi_hart_hang();
+  }
+}
diff --git a/src/sm.h b/src/sm.h
index 55161d4..91122de 100644
--- a/src/sm.h
+++ b/src/sm.h
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include "sm_err.h"
 
 void sm_init(bool cold_boot);
+void sm_restore_pmp(void);
 
 /* platform specific functions */
 #define ATTESTATION_KEY_LENGTH  64
-- 
